{{!
    @template mod_syllabus/date_select

    A real day/month/year date picker for use outside a mform (SCOPE §8 — "date-pickers
    reais em vez de <input type="date"> cru"), mirroring the day/month/year selects of
    core's own element-date_selector.mustache. Rendered as 3 empty <select> shells;
    amd/src/plan_dateselect.js fills their options and initial selection from
    data-timestamp — see that module for why the option lists are populated client-side
    instead of server-rendered (no simple translatable string exists for month names).

    Always invoke this scoped to its own sub-object via a Mustache section (see
    activity_row.mustache's startdatefield/enddatefield usage), so multiple instances on the
    same page never collide on variable names.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "fieldid": "syllabus-activity-startdate-5",
        "fieldclass": "syllabus-activity-startdate",
        "labeltext": "Data de início",
        "timestamp": 1749000000
    }
}}
<div class="syllabus-date-select {{fieldclass}}" data-timestamp="{{timestamp}}">
    <span class="form-label small mb-1 d-block" id="{{fieldid}}-label">{{labeltext}}</span>
    <div class="d-flex gap-1">
        <select class="form-select form-select-sm syllabus-date-day" aria-labelledby="{{fieldid}}-label"></select>
        <select class="form-select form-select-sm syllabus-date-month" aria-labelledby="{{fieldid}}-label"></select>
        <select class="form-select form-select-sm syllabus-date-year" aria-labelledby="{{fieldid}}-label"></select>
    </div>
</div>
